hadiths[28]{hadithnumber,text}:
"101","'A'isha reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him\npeace, said, \Jibril"
"102","Abu Shurayh al-Khuza'i reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \Anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day\nshould be good to his neighbours. Anyone who believes in Allah and the Last\nDay should be generous to his guest. Anyone who believes in Allah and the\nLast Day should be say what is good or be silent.\"""""
"103","Al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah\nbless him and grant him peace, asked his Companions about fornication and\nthey said, \It is unlawful. Allah and His Messenger have made it unlawful.\""\nHe said"
"104","Ibn 'Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \Jibril kept on recommending that I treat my\nneighbours well until I thought that he would order me to treat them as my\nheirs.\"""""
"105","Mujahid reported that a sheep was slaughtered for 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr.\nHe asked his slave, \Have you given any to our Jewish neighbour? Have you\ngiven any to our Jewish neighbour? I heard the Messenger of Allah"
"106","Muhammad ibn Salam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi informed us, saying: I heard Yahya ibn Sa'id say: Abu Bakr narrated to me, that Amrah narrated to him, that she heard Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""Gabriel kept advising me concerning the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir."""
"107","He told us Hajjaj bin Minhal, he said: Shu'bah told us, he said: Abu 'Imran informed me, he said: I heard Talhah, from 'A'ishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors, so to which of them should I give? He said: To the nearest of them to you in terms of door."
"108","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran al-Jawnī, from Talhah ibn 'Abd Allah, a man from Banu Taym ibn Murrah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors, to which of them should I give a gift? He said: To the one whose door is closest to you."
"109","Al-Hasan was asked about the neighbour and said, \The term 'neighbour'\nincludes the forty houses in front a person"
"110","Abu Hurayra said, \Do not begin with your more distant neighbours before\nthe closer ones. Rather begin with your nearest neighbours before the most\ndistant ones.\"""""
"111","Ibn 'Umar said, \There was a time when no one was more entitled to a\nperson's money than his Muslim brother. Now people love their dirhams and\ndinars more than their Muslim brother. I heard the Prophet"
"112","Ibn 'Abbas informed Ibn az-Zubayr, \I heard the Prophet"
"113","'Hear and obey, even\nif the ruler is a slave with his limbs amputated. When you cook a stew, put\na lot of water in it and then go and see the people of a neighbouring house\nand give them a reasonable amount of it. Pray the prayers at their proper\nprayers. Then if you find that the imam has already prayed, you have guarded\nyour prayer (by already having performed it). If not, it is a supererogatory\nprayer (since you have done it again).\""114"""
"114","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Abu Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, saying: Abu Imran narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: ""O Abu Dharr, when you cook broth, increase the water of the broth, and look after your neighbors, or give a portion to your neighbors."""
"115","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As reported that the Messenger of Allah,\nmay Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, \The best of companions in\nthe sight of Allah Almighty is the best of them towards his companion"
"116","Nafi' ibn 'Abdu'l-Harith reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \Part of the happiness of the Muslim man includes\na spacious dwelling"
"117","Abu Hurayra said, \Part of the supplication of the Prophet"
"118","Abu Musa reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \The Final Hour will not come until a man kills his\nneighbour"
"119","Here is the translated text in English:Hadith:Abu Hurayrah reported that the Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, there is a woman who spends the night in prayer and fasts during the day, and does good deeds, and gives charity, and is kind to her neighbors with her tongue?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, ""There is no good in her. She is from the people of the Fire."" They said, ""And what about a woman who is a worshipper, and gives charity, and does not harm anyone?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, ""She is from the people of Paradise."""
"120","'Umara ibn Ghurab reported that an aunt of his told him that she asked\n'A'isha, Umm al-Mu'minin, \If a woman's husband desires her and she refuses\nto give herself to him either because she is angry or not eager"
"121","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \A person whose neighbours are not safe from his\nevil will not enter the Garden.\"""""
"122","'Amr ibn Mu'adh al-Ashhali reported that his grandmother said, \The\nMessenger of Allah"
"123","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \Muslim women! Muslim women! A woman should not\ndisdain her female neighbour's gift"
"124","A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I have a neighbor who harms me. He said, ""Leave and take your belongings to the public road. He left and took his belongings, and the people gathered around him. They said, ""What is wrong with you?"" He said, ""I have a neighbor who harms me."" I mentioned it to the Prophet, and he said, ""Leave and take your belongings to the public road."" They would say, ""O Allah, curse him! O Allah, humble him."" He reached him, and the Prophet said, ""Return to your home, and by Allah, I will not harm you."""
"125","Abu Juhayfa said, \A man complained to the Prophet"
"126","Here is the translated text in English:

Hadith:

Makhled bin Malik narrated to us, saying: Abu Zuhair, 'Abd al-Rahman bin Maghrah, narrated to us, saying: Al-Fadl, meaning the son of Mubashshir, narrated to us, saying:

I heard Jabir say: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) seeking his help against his neighbor. While the man was sitting between the Rukn and the Maqam, the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned around and saw the man, who was standing with his clothes white, as if he were about to perform the funeral prayer. The Prophet (peace be upon him) then said: ""By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, who is the man you saw standing with his clothes white?"" He said: ""Have you seen him?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""You saw good, a great deal."" Then he said: ""That is Jibril, the Messenger of my Lord, who has been instructing me about my neighbor until I thought he was giving him an inheritance."""
"127","Thawban said, \When two men cut each other off for more than three days\nand one of them dies"
"128","Mujahid said, \I was with 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr while his slave was skinning\na sheep. He said"
